---
import cameras from '../data/cameras.json';import samples from '../data/samples.json';
import DeepGuide from './DeepGuide.astro';import FormatGuide from './FormatGuide.astro';import Layout from './Layout.astro';import Comparison from './Comparison.astro';import Calculator from './Calculator.astro';
---
<Layout home={true} locale={Astro.props.locale || 'en'} description={Astro.props.locale==='pt-br'?'Compare arquivos RAW e JPEG de câmeras reais, calcule espaço de armazenamento e encontre exemplos Canon, Sony e Nikon.':Astro.props.locale==='fr'?'Comparez les fichiers RAW et JPEG de vrais appareils et estimez votre stockage avec des exemples Canon, Sony et Nikon.':'Compare measured RAW camera samples, explore JPEG previews, and estimate photo storage with a free memory card calculator.'}><section class="hero wrap tool-intro"><h1>RAW vs JPEG: See the Difference & Choose Your Format</h1><p>Shoot RAW when you need editing flexibility or face difficult light; choose JPEG for smaller, ready-to-share files; save RAW + JPEG when you need both. Drag the slider to inspect real camera samples.</p></section><Comparison/><section class="wrap prose compact"><h2>RAW or JPEG: what is the difference?</h2><p>A RAW file preserves camera sensor information for processing, giving you greater control over white balance and tonal adjustments. A JPEG is already processed by the camera and uses lossy compression, making sharing and storage simpler. RAW does not automatically make every photograph look better: the camera, exposure and development decisions all matter.</p><p>These comparisons show a developed RAW image beside the JPEG preview embedded in the same RAW capture. That preview is not a separate full-resolution JPEG photograph or a controlled exposure-recovery test. <a href="/methodology/">See the exact method</a>.</p><h2>Measured RAW sizes from three cameras</h2><p>See the <a href="/cameras/">measured camera file-size chart</a>, or estimate how many photographs fit on a <a href="/memory-card-calculator/">32 GB–1 TB memory card</a>. Every RAW file size is linked to its original CC0 sample.</p></section><section class="wrap decision"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE QUICK DECISION</p><h2>Choose for the way you shoot.</h2></div><article><span class="format-tag">RAW</span><h3>Room to work.</h3><p>Keep sensor data for flexible editing. Useful when lighting is tricky, the shot matters, or you want control over the final look.</p></article><article><span class="format-tag">JPEG</span><h3>Ready to go.</h3><p>Smaller files with a finished look. Useful for fast sharing, simple workflows, and photographs you don’t plan to edit extensively.</p></article><article><span class="format-tag">RAW + JPEG</span><h3>A little of both.</h3><p>A ready-to-share image and an editable original. Convenient, with extra storage and more files to manage.</p></article></section><FormatGuide locale={Astro.props.locale || 'en'}/><Calculator/>{(!Astro.props.locale || Astro.props.locale==='en')&&<DeepGuide/>}<section id="camera-guides" class="wrap guides"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / CAMERA FIELD NOTES</p><h2>Start with your camera.</h2><p>Three measured samples. A dedicated guide for each camera.</p></div><div class="camera-guide-grid">{cameras.map(camera=><a class="guide-card" href={`/${samples.find(s=>s.id===camera.sampleId)!.slug}-raw-vs-jpeg/`}><span class="eyebrow">{samples.find(s=>s.id===camera.sampleId)!.brand.toUpperCase()}</span><h3>{camera.shortName}</h3><p>{camera.modeLabel}</p><p>{(samples.find(s=>s.id===camera.sampleId)!.rawBytes/1e6).toFixed(2)} MB · one measured RAW file</p><span class="guide-arrow">View sample & storage guide ↗</span></a>)}</div></section></Layout>
